WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:05.610
Audiences were shocked several times during
Avengers: Endgame, but it turns out the cast

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:09.980
may have been even more gobsmacked when watching
the superhero ensemble: It sounds like the

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:14.780
actors were told a blatant lie while shooting
one of the film's most gut-wrenching scenes.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:19.280
Warning: we're officially entering Spoiler
Country; population: you.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:23.900
Chatting with Jimmy Fallon during his May
1st appearance on The Tonight Show, Sebastian

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:29.430
Stan — the actor who plays Bucky Barnes
spilled a big secret: He and his Marvel co-stars

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:33.300
were told they were filming a wedding scene
for Avengers: Endgame… but it was actually

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.300
a sequence for the lakeside funeral of Tony
Stark.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:37.560
Major bummer!

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:42.540
The topic came up when Fallon asked Stan whether
he and his castmates had any idea what they

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.710
were filming, or the context of the lines
they were saying.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:47.760
"We did not for this one, we didn't.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:51.500
I mean, everything I filmed I found out on
the day."

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:55.900
Stan claims that he arrived on set one day
and noticed that everyone was dressed to the

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:56.480
nines.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.220
Of course he wondered why.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:03.360
"I was told there was a wedding… that there
was a wedding we were filming.

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:04.600
And I was like, 'Who's getting married?'"

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:10.080
Of course, Stan now realizes that this was
a complete and utter lie, and if you've seen

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:12.600
Avengers: Endgame, you already know why.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:16.340
"And then two people weren't there, so I guess
that was the bride and the groom."

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:21.060
Perhaps he phrased his comment this way so
that he didn't spoil the grim surprise for

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.420
the Tonight Show audience.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:27.720
But perhaps he was being totally serious and
actually believed Stark and Scarlett Johansson's

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.280
Black Widow were getting married.

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:35.140
As Marvel fans now know, Black Widow sacrificed
herself in order to save her fellow Avengers,

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:38.500
and Tony Stark also passed away after battling
Thanos.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:43.420
What Stan didn't realize is that the scene
was actually a funeral, not a wedding.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:48.280
Of course, it would be unusual for these two
characters to tie the knot in Endgame, especially

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:52.810
since Tony Stark and Gwyneth Paltrow's Pepper
Potts are raising their daughter Morgan throughout

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:53.320
the film.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:57.580
Maybe not coincidentally, marriage came up
in a separate interview with Bruce Banner

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:58.880
actor Mark Ruffalo.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:04.020
During that conversation, confirmed spoiler-spiller
Ruffalo claimed that Captain America ties

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:05.200
the knot in Endgame.

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:07.740
"He gets married in this!"

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:09.640
“Ha Ha, very funny.”

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:14.780
Now we know that this actually happens in
the film, after Steve Rogers decides to stay

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.640
in the past and marry Peggy Carter.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.680
Could Ruffalo have been referring to the same
scene that Stan discussed with Fallon?

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:25.060
On the other hand, Ruffalo admitted that he
received a script for Avengers: Endgame that

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:27.640
was full of scenes that aren't in the actual
move.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.240
"I didn't even get a whole script of this
movie.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.830
I don't know why.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:36.080
The script I did get had dummy scenes in it."

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:41.200
As he says in the interview, he assumed that
co-directors Joe and Anthony Russo included

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:44.080
the bogus wedding scene in order to throw
him off the scent.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:48.940
But Marvel actors are very familiar with hearing
lies and half-truths during production.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:54.200
Spider-Man actor Tom Holland once shared that
he had absolutely no idea what sequences he

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:56.240
was shooting for Avengers: Infinity War.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:00.400
"I was reading what I thought was a fake script
because it was like, 'Spider-Man's in space!'

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.860
So I didn't finish it, but I found out it
was real."

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:08.840
Scarlet Witch actress Elizabeth Olsen claims
that they filmed the disintegration of even

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:12.100
more characters in Infinity War than the ones
we see onscreen.

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:16.940
What's more, Ruffalo also revealed that they
had him film five very different endings to

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:17.520
the film.

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:21.900
When the Russo brothers loosen their grip
on spoilers after it's clear that the entire

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:26.210
universe has finally seen the film, perhaps
we'll learn even more secrets from behind

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:26.820
the scenes.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:29.720
Was Chris Hemsworth playing Fortnite between
takes?

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:34.740
Did Chris Evans need to wear butt pads in
order to turn Captain America's backside into

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:35.240
America's…

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:40.060
On second thought, we'll leave that particular
plot point unspoiled for you.

